# Build the production image from source only. Excludes paths a `next build`
# and the runtime never need — keeping secrets, local CLI state, and scratch
# tooling out of the image (smaller, and no keys/seeds baked in).
#
# NOTE: do NOT add `.env` here — the build inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* from it.
#
# `node_modules` IS excluded (2026-09-14). The note that previously lumped it in
# with `.env` gave "reinstalls deps inside the container" as the reason, which is
# an argument for excluding it, not keeping it: there is no Dockerfile, servel
# auto-detects and runs the install itself, so the 2.9 GB we were uploading was
# discarded. Two deploys that day died mid-upload with "use of closed network
# connection" before the build ever started. If a build ever fails for a missing
# dependency, put it back — a failed build cannot take prod down, the running
# version keeps serving.

.git
.next
node_modules

# Secrets / local CLI state — must never enter the image.
.keys
.servel
.env*.local
private

# Local scratch + probe scripts (not part of the app; also what broke the
# build before the ES2020 target bump). Matches the top-level dir only.
scripts

# Rust/Soroban build output for the bond-escrow contract: `target/debug` alone
# is 848 MB across 1954 files (2026-09-26), and it was the whole reason the
# build context sat at 302 MB. `.gitignore:54` already ignores it — which did
# NOT help, because servel packages the tree minus `.dockerignore` and does not
# read `.gitignore` at all. Hence the duplicate entry here. Nothing under `src/`
# reads `contracts/` (only doc-comment mentions), so the Next build never needs
# it. Excluding this plus `.worktrees` takes the context from 928 MB to 23 MB.
# `contracts/*/target` rather than a literal path so a second contract is covered.
contracts/*/target

# Git worktrees for in-flight branches — other branches' full trees, not this
# app's source. Their node_modules/.next are already matched above.
.worktrees

# OS / editor / logs
*.log
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
